{
  "version": "1",
  "description": "Cross-language redaction conformance corpus. Every SDK MUST pass every case. The Rust implementation in fasten-core/src/redact.rs is canonical. Input and expected are JSON-serialisable objects. Value-shape tests use the neutral key 'note' so key-pattern redaction does not interfere. NOTE: The Stripe live-key case (sk_live_[A-Za-z0-9]{24,}) is intentionally absent — JSON cannot use string concatenation so the literal would trigger GitHub push protection. Each SDK covers it via a runtime-constructed test in its own test suite.",
  "replacement": "***",
  "cases": [
